WEBVTT

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.700
Sorry, was I late?

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.130
No, I just arrived a little while ago.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.930
I'm sorry for asking you to come when you're so busy.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.130
I really appreciate it.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:59.910
Don't worry about it.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.120
I don't think I'll be of much help, though.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.320
I wonder if Ohno-san and everyone else are already in line.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.600
I heard they came on the first train yesterday.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.060
On the first day? That's amazing.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:14.940
They probably did the same thing today since they
planned to spend the entire weekend looking around.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.220
They sure have a lot of stamina, as expected of fujoshi.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.790
Shouldn't they be feeling jet lag?

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.350
It's a matter of willpower.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.700
What female otakus have plenty of is willpower, not stamina.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:28.750
I see.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.880
I arrived around noon yesterday,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.470
and when I ran into them at a
certain section,
Suzy really glared at me.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:45.930
I'm not sure whether she meant that it was
about time I came or if she was marking her territory.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.720
It seems like that girl's trying to act morose.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.110
She might have thought of you as a rival, Ogiue-san.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.270
It's not like I'm trying to play that role.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.330
You're right. Sorry.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:00.740
That's okay.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.380
The people are like garbage!

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.300
We know, so don't say that.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.180
She probably knows exactly what she's saying.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:25.900
Barusu!

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.480
Shut up, Sue!

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.140
Oh, this is it.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.260
Yeah.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:36.730
Go ahead.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.930
How's it look?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.220
There's nothing wrong with the printing.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.040
You're not allowed to look.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.420
I know.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.620
If you take so much as a peek, you'll be cursed.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.020
You're not even allowed to touch it.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.370
I can't be much of a vendor, can I?

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.840
You'll manage.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.220
<i>Even though the majority of people
here are women, I don't feel alienated.</i>

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.520
<i>I guess ignoring me is their way of dealing with it.</i>

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.070
Is this okay?

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.310
Yeah, it looks fine.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.320
Oh, if there's any circle you want to visit, please do so now.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.030
Yeah, but there's no need to be hasty.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.810
We're not allowed to look around before it's officially
open, and I have plenty of time to do that when we're done.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.720
I see.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:39.460
<i>We hereby commence the
second day
of the 68th Comic Festival.</i>

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.930
This area's pretty calm.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.570
It's probably still a little too early for a crowd.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.270
I guess so.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:55.320
The people who are interested in
female-oriented Kujiun books are absolute fanatics,

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.460
since the original manga's aimed toward males.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.150
There are a lot of men here, though.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:05.790
It might be because a transvestite Chihiro's a potential theme.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:12.220
I still have mixed feelings about that since
the original manga was drawn by a female artist.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.040
Please take a look.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.000
Oh, thanks.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.140
Thank you.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.440
T-Thank you.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.480
<i>It wasn't any good.</i>

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.040
Let's just relax and take it easy.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:36.980
Well, okay.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:42.150
I'm sorry for making you do all the talking, Sasahara-san.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.290
It's not a problem.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.260
I'll make sure to say something next time.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.280
You don't have to tell me that.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.320
Excuse me, I'm going to take a break.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.240
Nice work.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.440
She's pretty tough.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.030
Angela plays a lot of sports.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.700
She has a nice abdomen.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.480
That aside, I'm glad I was able to finish it in time.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.880
The patterns and the rest of the design were different from yours, Ohno-san.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.930
I'm more bustier than her, though.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.880
Tanaka-san, feel free to take a lot of pictures.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.830
Thanks, but I don't think I can do that.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:54.310
I brought a camera with me,
but it feels like I might collapse at any time.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:59.130
Kanako, come on! Interpret!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.670
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.560
Don't call me so loudly.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.230
I'd like a copy.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.580
Oh, thank you very much.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.930
That'll be five hundred yen.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.200
Thank you very much.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.800
How do you feel about making your first sale, sensei?

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:29.240
How should I describe it?
It exceeded my expectations.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:29.800
I see.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.220
I'm going to the restroom.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.200
Oh, okay.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.130
<i>Wow, that was close.</i>

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.970
<i>I was staring right at him because...</i>

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.890
<i>he looked so happy.</i>

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.100
Please proceed carefully!

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.790
Yukimian-san, I'd like a copy, nya!

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.740
Oh, sure. Thank you very much.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.320
Aren't you going to check the content?

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.400
It's okay, nya.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:43.220
It's past noon already. I wonder why Sue hasn't come back.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:45.250
Oh, don't worry.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:49.050
I think she's just walking around to see everything.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.890
She's so thorough, you know.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:57.640
But she stands out in a crowd. I hope she'll be okay.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.350
She'll be just fine.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.240
<i>I wonder how Sasahara-san's doing.</i>

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:09.130
Is selling two books after an hour good or bad?

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.400
Well,

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.240
it's pretty good for a first-time participant.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.720
I guess so.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.690
Dissatisfied?

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:19.160
No, it's not that.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:23.180
Here.

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:34.450
I was a little hesitant at first, but I'm glad I came.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:44.470
I felt like I was a worthless, hopeless human
being after blowing one interview after another.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.980
Right now, I feel as if I belong here.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.310
Is looking for a job that difficult?

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:53.770
Difficult? Yeah, that's one way to put it.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:59.900
Of course I'm not the only one struggling,
but it isn't difficult to end up thinking about yourself.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:05.910
This is the end of the Pushuke line.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:06.390
Didn't he pull three all-nighters in a row?

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.700
Please line up here.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.840
How does he look so energetic?

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:16.380
In other words, the interviewer is higher up on
the corporate ladder with each successive interview?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:23.960
Yeah, the final obstacle's an interview with the president, but I think I was rejected one or two tiers below that.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.180
That's difficult to accept.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:30.490
Yeah. I'd prefer if somebody actually
involved with the work turned me down.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:32.980
I'd just give up after that.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.780
There's no way an executive can
properly evaluate a person's aptitude.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.030
What about you, Ogiue-san?

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.990
Do you want to become a manga artist?

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:47.950
I never thought about making a career out of drawing manga,

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:52.990
although I do draw it as if I was possessed.

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:53.880
All the time, really.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.340
You're the type of person who
becomes one without thinking about it.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.920
Is that so?

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:06.110
Those who aren't able to make it are
the ones who ask others how they did it.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.640
Being able to draw manga,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.690
becoming a manga artist,

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:15.720
and making a living out of drawing manga are entirely different.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.200
Yeah.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:20.450
Ogiue-san, you're already a manga artist.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.410
It's true that I've always
drawn since I was a child.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.420
A child prodigy, huh?

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.830
Ogiue?

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.430
It is you, Ogiue!

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:42.620
No way!

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:46.760
It was hard to recognize you
without your glasses.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:49.270
<i>I wonder if they're her friends from home.</i>

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:54.360
I heard you went to Tokyo,
but who would've thought I'd meet you in a place like this?

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:58.530
Oh, is this Ogiue's book? Amazing!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.890
You're still drawing these kinds of things, huh?

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.010
Yeah.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:06.790
I'll buy it, I'll buy it. Five hundred yen?

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.980
It's okay, you can have it.

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:09.990
Are you sure?

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.090
Yeah, it's all yours.

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:12.000
Thanks.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.500
Oh, hello.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.820
Boyfriend?

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:16.980
No!

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.960
<i>Wow, how blunt.</i>

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.010
<i>What is it?</i>

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.360
Oh, well. Thanks for the doujinshi.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.560
Thanks.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.760
Take care.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:29.310
Bye!

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:35.130
Sorry about the rude comments.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:36.930
No, that's okay.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:37.980
Are they your friends from home?

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.400
They're friends from middle school.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.240
Friends?

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:48.660
It might be more accurate to say that
they just share the same interests as me.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:52.450
Ogiue-san?

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.170
Sorry, I'm not feeling well.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.730
Do you want to go to the infirmary?

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.990
No, I'll be fine after I get a little rest.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.140
It's more mental than it is physical.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:05.960
<i>Mental?</i>

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:09.690
<i>Did something happen between
her and the people who stopped by?</i>

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.250
<i>Shouldn't things that happened during
middle school be distant memories by now?</i>

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.310
A blonde.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:17.420
She's cute.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.300
A foreigner.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:19.520
Real life Pinky: Q?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:20.730
She's cute.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.370
What should we do?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.540
Well, there's nothing we can do.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.580
If she likes it, she can buy it.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.820
If she wants it, I'll give it to her.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.390
I mean... I don't need... I'll give it to you.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.880
I mean...

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.200
N-No money.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.550
I don't think that's quite right.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:54.830
H-How do I say it?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.210
You sound like Kucchii.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:56.980
What?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:03.040
No money... It's not coming out at all.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.000
M-Money... Money...

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:17.930
O-O-O-O-Ohno-senpai... call her!
I mean I'll go get her!

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:22.250
I don't know where she is, and that would take too much time.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.010
She's probably at the cosplay plaza.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:30.140
How should I say it?

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.390
I have to say that I'll give it to her.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:35.350
Let's see... Present for you.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:37.810
Thanks.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.510
Did she understand what you said?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:55.120
I think so, since she said thanks.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.500
How are you feeling?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.690
Are you okay?

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:03.880
Oh, I completely forgot about it.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.640
I mean...

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.740
It sounds like I'm definitely lying.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.470
No, you said it was a mental problem.

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:14.440
That's why...

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.570
Sorry for making you worry.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.560
It's okay, but...

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.710
Hey!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.360
Madarame-san!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.020
I decided to stop by.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.660
What about work?

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.390
You said you were busy today.

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.500
I took a half-day leave.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.880
You did?

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.930
Oh, Mugi x Sen?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.740
If you touch it, you'll be cursed.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:36.280
I guarantee it.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.030
How come?

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:39.470
You just will!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.930
Sign please.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.880
This page is awesome. Real hardcore.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.490
<i>On purpose? Is she doing this on purpose?</i>

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.150
<i>Is it intentional?</i>

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:59.930
I don't have a fancy autograph or anything,

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:02.140
but I'll sign it for you on the cover.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:07.570
<i>She's definitely not like me at all.</i>

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.450
Angela, has Sue called you?

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.490
Oh, no, she hasn't.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.850
Isn't this a little too much?

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:25.380
Oh, it's Ogiue-san.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.040
Hello? What?

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.970
It looks like she's relaxing at our booth.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.070
Please put Sue on the phone.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.550
<i>Change please.</i>

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.460
<i>Yes?</i>

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.890
What are you doing there?
Come back.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.700
<i>Are you listening to me?</i>

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.440
Sue, come back! Quick!

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.800
We have to leave those two alone.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.780
<i>Ohno-san?</i>

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:58.060
<i>Sasahara-san?
Aren't you going to celebrate after the Comifes is over?</i>

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:58.740
I am?

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.080
Of course you are!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.230
<i>Hold on, I'll hand the phone to Ogiue-san.</i>

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:03.160
No, don't!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:04.920
What?

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.990
<i>I'll have Sue leave at once.</i>

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:09.130
Okay, but aren't we going together?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.070
No, we're not.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.130
I mean we are, but still...

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.500
<i>Can I go, too?</i>

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.960
Madarame-san?

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.810
I'm a woman!

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:25.770
I love the ocean!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.090
Stop it!

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:27.360
All right, Sue!

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.980
We're not at the Comic Festival anymore!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.580
Flat chests are a symbol of status.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.850
Kanako, never mind, let go.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:53.340
She's just a bit too excited cause she likes Chika so much.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.720
My first plan has failed.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:59.550
Are you talking about Kanji and Chika?

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:04.020
Why has it turned out like this?

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.250
Isn't this a deus ex machina?

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.790
Yeah.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:11.050
Speaking of which, where's Kuchiki-kun?

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.030
He left as soon as he finished purchasing his books.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.450
Kousaka was at the Pushuke booth.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.560
Oh, really?

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.070
Didn't you talk to him?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:24.500
Yeah. He was busy with work, so I decided against it.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.010
Did he look alright?

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.700
His job must be pretty tough.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:32.270
To tell you the truth, he looked like his usual self.

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.020
He might have been a little more cheerful than that.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.930
Amazing. He's something else.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:41.920
I wonder what Kugayama-san's doing.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.520
It's rare for him not to stop by the Comifes.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:57.480
You can't get out until you count to a hundred.

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:02.060
<i>Ohno-san sounds like their mother.</i>

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.240
<i>I wonder why.</i>

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.960
You're still drawing these kinds of things, huh?

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:15.800
You're the type of person who
becomes one without thinking about it.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:41.200
Please do something!
She won't stop following me!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.470
What's wrong with that?

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:48.240
It's a rare sight to see Sue that attached to someone.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.880
She really must have liked your book, Ogiue-san.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:53.670
Did you read it?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:54.920
Of course.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.960
yeah, so have I! Chika, your book is great,

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:07.010
especially when Mugio splashes sperm onto Chihiro's glasses!

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.510
She's praising your work.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.600
Angela has a fetish for glasses.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.650
Really?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.480
A fetish for glasses, huh?

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:21.030
I heard that Genshiken's made a book before.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.460
Can I take a look?

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:25.780
She's asking if she can take a look at the book you made last time, Sasahara-san.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.450
Well, it's a male-oriented book, so...

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:35.040
No problem, I love both girls and boys.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:38.750
She said that she doesn't care
whether it's aimed at fujoshis or otakus.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.210
N-N-N-No, that's a little unreasonable!

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:45.800
Give me a break!
The person who drew it already graduated, too.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:50.140
What? Are they strict about copyrights in Japan?

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.790
Step in cat shit!

00:20:54.320 --> 00:21:00.030
<i>Angela and Suzy went back to
America the day after the Comifes.</i>

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:05.640
<i>The myriad of doujinshi they purchased
was to be sent to them later by Ohno-san.</i>

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:40.850
<i>Circle Yukimian's first publication: Right By Your Side.</i>

00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:42.450
<i>Total copies made: fifty.</i>

00:22:42.450 --> 00:22:43.960
<i>Copies distributed: eleven.</i>

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:45.550
<i>In stock: thirty-nine.</i>

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:11.460
What was the best final episode?

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.290
It had to be Nekozaemon.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.570
Oh, you mean how ○○ta does everything by himself?

00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:19.670
What about The Dog of Flanders?

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:22.850
Even though it hasn't been made yet, I bet Garakame will be a classic.

00:23:22.850 --> 00:23:26.630
One of my favorite last episodes has to be
the one with the quote, "I couldn't be happier."

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.920
My favorite final episode is...

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:33.170
Our battle has just begun!

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:37.260
Yes, an ambiguous ending is the best kind of ending!
